userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: When a stopcock connecting a flask of H2 to a flask of O2 is opened, random molecular motion drives both gases down their own concentration gradients until they are uniformly mixed — and the lighter H2 spreads across faster than the heavier O2.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Diffusion needs no driving force beyond random motion: gases spread until concentrations even out, and because lighter molecules move faster at the same temperature, H2 mixes into the O2 flask noticeably sooner than O2 mixes back — the qualitative picture behind Graham's law.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

