<p style="margin:0 0 2px 0;font-weight:bold;font-size:13px">Diffusion of H₂ and O₂</p>
<p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;max-width:270px;color:#333">Pure H₂ fills the left bulb and pure O₂ the right; the closed valve keeps them completely separated, so each gas sits at maximum concentration gradient across the neck.</p>
<span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px"><button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button><span id="stepLabel" style="font-size:11.5px">1 / 4 · Stopcock closed</span><button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button></span>
<label>Elapsed time after stopcock opens: <output id="elapsedTimeVal">0</output>
<input id="elapsedTimeInput" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="0" oninput="document.getElementById('elapsedTimeVal').value=this.value;update_elapsedTime(+this.value)"></label>
<button id="playBtn" onclick="trigger_playDiffusion()">▶ Play diffusion</button>
<label><input id="massViewInput" type="checkbox" onchange="toggle_massView(this.checked)"> Color-code by molar mass</label>
<p style="margin:2px 0 0 0;font-size:11px;color:#666;line-height:1.45">Hover a molecule, a bulb or the stopcock for details; click for a short explanation. Click panels (a)–(c) below the apparatus to jump to that stage.</p>
